{'type': 'chat_message', 'role': {'type': 'role', 'value': 'assistant'}, 'contents': [{'type': 'text', 'text': '### **Delegation Brief for Specialist Agents**\n\n**User Request:**  \n"Hi there, I want to go to New York. Create a planner itinerary."\n\nThis means the user wishes to create a detailed itinerary for a trip to New York City. The planner should include activities, accommodations, transportation, meals, and other relevant details to ensure an enjoyable and well-organized travel experience.  \n\n### Assigned Roles for the Agents:  \n\n### **1. Requirements Analyst**  \n**Purpose:** Understand and clarify the unique needs and preferences for the New York trip and define the scope for the itinerary.  \n\n**Tasks:**\n- Engage with the user to gather key information:\n  - Travel dates (arrival and departure times).\n  - Budget for the trip (e.g., budget-friendly, mid-range, or luxury).\n  - Interests and preferences (e.g., sightseeing, shopping, dining, cultural experiences, nightlife, etc.).\n  - Group size (solo, couple, family, or group traveling together).\n  - Specific neighborhoods or attractions they wish to visit (e.g., Times Square, Central Park, Statue of Liberty, Broadway).\n  - Accommodation preferences (hotel, hostel, Airbnb, etc.).\n  - Dietary restrictions or preferences for meals.\n  - Transportation requirements (e.g., subway usage, taxis, walking, biking).\n- Define the daily structure of the itinerary (e.g., how packed or relaxed the schedule should be).\n- Provide detailed requirements for the implementation specialist to deliver the itinerary.\n\n**Deliverable:**  \nA comprehensive requirements document outlining all user needs, covering timelines, activities, budget constraints, and personalized preferences.  \n\n---\n\n### **2. Implementation Specialist**  \n**Purpose:** Design the itinerary based on the requirements document provided by the analyst, ensuring practicality, accuracy, and alignment with the user’s preferences.  \n\n**Tasks:**\n- Research and arrange details for each day of the trip:\n  - Select accommodations that fit the user\'s budget and location preferences.\n  - Plan daily activities, including time slots for visits to iconic landmarks, cultural attractions, shopping districts, and dining options.  \n  - Optimize routes and timing for transportation within New York City to minimize travel hassles.\n  - Identify must-visit restaurants or cafes for meal options while accommodating any dietary restrictions.  \n  - Include alternatives for weather, busy periods, or sudden changes.\n- Ensure the user’s itinerary is evenly paced with options for breaks, flexible plans, or spontaneous explorations.  \n- Incorporate booking links (e.g., hotels, restaurants, tours) if required.\n- Add practical advice (e.g., subway tips, safety recommendations, weather-related packing).  \n\n**Deliverable:**  \nA finalized itinerary in an organized format, ready for the user to follow, including all logistical details like locations, timings, and any necessary reservations links or operational tips.\n\n---\n\n### **Process Flow:**  \n1. **Requirements Analyst** works with the user to gather information and provide it to the Implementation Specialist.  \n2. **Implementation Specialist** designs and finalizes the itinerary based on the gathered requirements.  \n3. The team synthesizes their work into the final itinerary to deliver an optimal plan for the trip to New York City.  \n\nLet me know if I should clarify further for the agents!'}], 'additional_properties': {}}
