e comparison tables for easy evaluation.  \n- **Booking Support:** Use agent-friendly booking systems if required (ensure compliance with policies).\n\n---\n\n#### **Validation Steps:**\n1. Check pricing and details from multiple platforms.  \n2. Ensure filters align with user preferences: timing, direct routes, economic seating.  \n3. Verify direct booking links or user-friendly access for self-service bookings.  \n4. Ensure full transparency on inclusions (e.g., meal, baggage).\n\n---\n\n#### **Deliverable:**  \nA **comprehensive flight summary** (~1 page) listing 2–3 options with clear comparison points:\n- Airline name and flight number.  \n- Departure and arrival times.  \n- Duration of the flight.  \n- Price and inclusions (baggage, meals).  \n- Booking links.  \n\nProvide quick notes on each option with alignment to user preferences.\n\n---\n\n---\n\n### **Process Workflow & Final Refinement**\n1. **Requirements Analyst and Implementation Specialist Communication:**  \n   - Initial requirements document from Analyst \u2192 Provided to Specialist.  \n2. **Implementation Specialist outputs:**  \n   - Adds detailed comparisons and guidance in the finalized flight summary.  \n\n---\n\n### Key Quality Checks:\nBefore submitting the final deliverable:  \n- Ensure accuracy in travel information (route, date, filters).  \n- Validate affordability and inclusions with respect to "economic seating."  \n- Confirm booking links are functional and user-accessible.  \n\nLet me know if you’d like Azure workflows integrated for internal collaboration!'}], 'additional_properties': {}}
