.  \n2. **Data Preparation Workflow:** The Foundry must successfully ingest, clean, transform, and process data from user-specified sources via scalable Azure data preparation services.  \n3. **Model Training Pipeline:** Training workflows (using custom or prebuilt models) must support automation, adjustable hyperparameters, and validation steps aligned with business goals.  \n4. **Deployment and Monitoring:** Models must successfully deploy via Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) endpoints or Azure-managed services and include real-time monitoring of performance metrics.  \n5. **Security Compliance:** Foundry must implement encrypted data handling, role-based access controls (RBAC), and secure connection mechanisms for compliance.  \n6. **Scalability:** The Foundry architecture must support horizontal scaling of resources and workflows, ensuring fast adaptation to increased workloads or datasets.  \n7. **Testing and Validation:** Pre-deployment testing and simulation of AI workflows must yield reliable results for training, deployment, and monitoring.  \n8. **Usability and Documentation:** Instructions must be clear and actionable, enabling users to operate Foundry components seamlessly with minimal technical effort.  \n\nBy achieving these criteria, the Azure AI Foundry provides a robust, scalable, and high-performing AI/ML lifecycle management solution tailored to user needs.'}], 'author_name': 'DevUI-Requirements-Agent', 'additional_properties': {}}
